        "content": "Handling Errors & Exceptions",
        "type": "heading",
        "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content2": {
        "content": "Graceful error handling improves user experience and helps you diagnose issues in production.",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content3": {
        "content": "1. Try-Catch",
        "type": "sub-heading",
        "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content4": {
        "content": "Use `try-catch` blocks to handle synchronous and asynchronous errors.",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content5": {
        "content": "try {\n  await apiCall();\n} catch (e) {\n  print('Error: $e');\n}",
        "type": "code",
        "typeOf": "code"
    },
    "content6": {
        "content": "2. Global Error Handling",
        "type": "sub-heading",
        "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content7": {
        "content": "Catch errors that aren't caught by try-catch blocks using `FlutterError.onError` and `PlatformDispatcher.instance.onError`.",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content8": {
        "content": "Summary",
        "type": "heading",
        "typeOf": "Text"
    },
    "content9": {
        "content": "Always show a user-friendly message when something goes wrong, instead of crashing the app.",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "typeOf": "Text"
    },
